WEBVTT

00:02.563 --> 00:04.314
Water.

00:04.691 --> 00:06.316
Earth.

00:06.859 --> 00:08.694
Fire.

00:09.028 --> 00:10.529
Air.

00:11.114 --> 00:15.033
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

00:15.368 --> 00:18.912
Then everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

00:19.747 --> 00:22.374
Only the Avatar,
master of all four elements,

00:22.458 --> 00:23.709
could stop them.

00:23.918 --> 00:25.460
But when the world needed him most,

00:25.586 --> 00:27.087
he vanished.

00:27.422 --> 00:31.216
100 years passed, and my brother and I
discovered the new Avatar,

00:31.301 --> 00:32.968
an airbender named Aang.

00:33.177 --> 00:35.304
And although his airbending
skills are great,

00:35.388 --> 00:37.889
he has a lot to learn before
he's ready to save anyone.

00:37.974 --> 00:38.974
Unh!

00:39.058 --> 00:42.019
But I believe Aang can save the world.

01:04.167 --> 01:06.293
Hey, look!
A sword made out of a whale's tooth!

01:06.502 --> 01:07.586
Let me see that.

01:18.222 --> 01:19.681
This is a Water Tribe weapon.

01:19.807 --> 01:21.475
See if you can find anything else.

01:22.977 --> 01:24.269
Did someone lose something?

01:24.437 --> 01:25.645
No, we found something.

01:29.025 --> 01:30.150
It's burned.

01:31.319 --> 01:33.153
There was a battle.

01:33.404 --> 01:35.697
Water Tribe warriors ambushed
a group of firebenders.

01:36.157 --> 01:37.783
The firebenders fought back,

01:37.909 --> 01:39.409
but the warriors
drove them down this hill.

01:46.167 --> 01:47.626
So then what happened?

01:47.710 --> 01:49.544
I don't know. The trail ends here.

01:49.754 --> 01:51.380
Wait! Look!

01:52.131 --> 01:53.840
It's one of our boats!

01:55.718 --> 01:57.260
Is this dad's boat?

01:57.470 --> 01:59.846
No, but it's from his fleet.

02:00.056 --> 02:01.098
Dad was here.

02:06.354 --> 02:08.063
See, Prince Zuko?

02:08.147 --> 02:11.733
A moment of quiet is good
for your mental well-being.

02:12.819 --> 02:14.694
Unh!

02:16.280 --> 02:18.281
Watch out!

02:18.366 --> 02:19.491
Get back!

02:19.575 --> 02:20.742
We're after a stowaway.

02:20.910 --> 02:22.619
There are no stowaways on my ship.

02:38.094 --> 02:39.678
He's paralyzed.

02:39.762 --> 02:41.263
Only temporarily.

02:41.514 --> 02:43.056
The toxins will wear off
in about an hour.

02:43.141 --> 02:44.433
But by then, he'll be in jail,

02:44.517 --> 02:45.892
and I'll have my money.

02:46.018 --> 02:47.686
But how did you find him on my ship?

02:48.104 --> 02:51.189
My shirshu can smell a rat
a continent away.

02:51.524 --> 02:53.108
Well, I'm impressed.

02:57.613 --> 02:59.990
Very impressed.

03:18.968 --> 03:19.968
Sokka.

03:20.052 --> 03:21.094
I'm coming with you.

03:21.429 --> 03:23.972
You're not old enough to go to war,
Sokka. You know that.

03:24.765 --> 03:26.433
I'm strong. I'm brave.

03:26.559 --> 03:27.976
I can fight!

03:28.060 --> 03:29.436
Please, dad?

03:29.979 --> 03:32.481
Being a man is knowing
where you're needed the most,

03:32.940 --> 03:36.151
and for you right now,
that's here protecting your sister.

03:36.861 --> 03:38.320
I don't understand.

03:38.529 --> 03:40.447
Someday you will.

03:41.407 --> 03:43.325
I'm gonna miss you so much.

03:49.499 --> 03:50.624
Who's there?

03:51.751 --> 03:52.834
Sokka?

03:52.919 --> 03:53.919
Bato?

03:54.086 --> 03:55.504
Who the what now?

03:55.713 --> 03:56.755
Bato!

03:56.964 --> 03:59.549
Sokka! Katara!

03:59.759 --> 04:01.760
It is so good to see you two.

04:01.844 --> 04:04.513
You've grown so much.

04:04.722 --> 04:06.014
Hi, I'm Aang.

04:06.224 --> 04:07.432
-Where's dad?
-Is he here?

04:07.767 --> 04:09.434
No. He and the other warriors

04:09.519 --> 04:12.270
should be in the eastern
Earth Kingdom by now.

04:15.107 --> 04:16.483
This is no place for a reunion.

04:16.651 --> 04:17.901
Let's get inside.

04:23.699 --> 04:24.991
After I was wounded,

04:25.076 --> 04:26.993
your father carried me to this abbey.

04:28.079 --> 04:30.747
The sisters
have cared for me ever since.

04:30.831 --> 04:33.250
Superior, these are Hakoda's children.

04:33.334 --> 04:35.210
They've been traveling
with the Avatar.

04:35.545 --> 04:36.836
I found them by my boat.

04:37.046 --> 04:39.589
Young Avatar, it gives me great joy

04:39.674 --> 04:40.882
to be in your presence.

04:41.217 --> 04:43.009
Welcome to our abbey.

04:43.386 --> 04:45.679
Thank you.
It's truly an honor to be here.

04:45.972 --> 04:47.055
If there's anything--

04:47.265 --> 04:48.348
What smells so good, Bato?

04:49.767 --> 04:52.185
The sisters craft ointments
and perfumes.

04:52.478 --> 04:55.230
Perfume? Maybe we could
dump some on Appa,

04:55.314 --> 04:56.690
because he stinks so much.

04:56.774 --> 04:58.191
Am I right?

05:00.528 --> 05:01.820
You have your father's wit.

05:03.864 --> 05:06.116
Bato, it looks like home!

05:06.492 --> 05:08.868
Everything's here, even the pelts.

05:08.953 --> 05:12.581
Yeah. Nothing's cozier
than dead animal skins.

05:15.084 --> 05:16.334
Ack!

05:18.879 --> 05:21.923
No way! Stewed sea prunes?

05:22.133 --> 05:24.009
Help yourself.

05:24.218 --> 05:26.177
Dad could eat
a whole barrel of these things.

05:29.473 --> 05:32.809
Bato, is it true you
and dad lassoed an arctic hippo?

05:33.060 --> 05:34.436
It was your father's idea.

05:34.520 --> 05:36.187
He just dragged me along.

05:36.272 --> 05:38.231
Well, the hippo did the dragging.

05:38.441 --> 05:40.191
Hey, I ride animals, too!

05:40.276 --> 05:42.193
One time, there was
this giant eel, and I--

05:42.278 --> 05:44.779
So, who was it that came up
with the great blubber fiasco?

05:44.864 --> 05:46.364
You knew about that?

05:46.574 --> 05:47.866
Everyone does.

05:47.950 --> 05:49.200
What's that story?

05:49.285 --> 05:50.327
It's a long one, Aang.

05:50.411 --> 05:51.536
Some other time.

05:51.621 --> 05:54.331
You and dad had
so many hilarious adventures.

05:54.707 --> 05:57.292
Not all of which
were hilarious at the time,

05:57.376 --> 05:59.794
but everything's funny with hindsight.

05:59.879 --> 06:00.920
Aang!

06:01.005 --> 06:04.299
Please put that down.
It's ceremonial and very fragile.

06:05.635 --> 06:08.178
Was it you or dad
that put an octopus on your head

06:08.262 --> 06:09.929
and convinced gran-gran
you were a water spirit?

06:10.097 --> 06:13.683
Your dad wore the octopus,
but I did the spooky voice.

06:16.270 --> 06:17.896
Aah! Unh...

06:27.531 --> 06:29.824
Out of my way! Step aside, filth.

06:29.909 --> 06:31.785
He means no offense.

06:31.994 --> 06:34.329
I'm certain you bathe regularly.

06:34.830 --> 06:36.081
I need to talk to you.

06:36.290 --> 06:38.333
Well, if it isn't my new friends,

06:38.542 --> 06:40.543
Angry Boy and Uncle Lazy.

06:40.753 --> 06:42.379
Heh heh heh!

06:49.303 --> 06:50.887
Your beast trashed my ship.

06:50.971 --> 06:52.263
You have to pay me back.

06:52.598 --> 06:53.973
Well, I'd love to help you out,

06:54.058 --> 06:55.475
but I'm a little short on money.

06:55.685 --> 06:56.976
Drinks on me!

07:02.066 --> 07:04.025
Money isn't what I had in mind.

07:06.153 --> 07:07.779
I need you to find someone.

07:07.988 --> 07:10.448
What happened?
Your girlfriend run off on you?

07:10.825 --> 07:12.200
It's not the girl I'm after.

07:12.284 --> 07:13.785
It's the bald monk
she's traveling with.

07:14.328 --> 07:15.787
Whatever you say.

07:15.871 --> 07:17.330
If you find them,

07:17.415 --> 07:19.999
I'll consider the damage
to my ship paid for.

07:20.167 --> 07:21.918
Ha! Forget it.

07:22.002 --> 07:24.754
Plus, we'll pay your weight in gold.

07:25.214 --> 07:27.966
Make it your weight,
and we got a deal.

07:28.342 --> 07:30.468
Ha ha ha! You got it!

07:30.553 --> 07:31.594
Get on!

07:44.316 --> 07:46.151
There's something
I should tell you kids.

07:46.736 --> 07:48.528
I'm expecting a message
from your father.

07:48.821 --> 07:50.780
-Really?
-When?

07:50.990 --> 07:52.282
Any day now.

07:52.366 --> 07:53.950
Your father said he'd send a message

07:54.034 --> 07:55.744
when they found the rendezvous point.

07:55.953 --> 07:58.037
If you wait here
until the message arrives,

07:58.247 --> 08:00.790
you can come with me
and see your father again.

08:01.000 --> 08:03.418
It's been over two years
since we've seen dad.

08:03.627 --> 08:04.961
That would be so incredible.

08:05.045 --> 08:06.045
Katara!

08:06.380 --> 08:07.672
I do really miss him.

08:08.090 --> 08:09.924
It would be great to see dad.

08:10.009 --> 08:12.427
It's been far too long,
hasn't it?

08:13.471 --> 08:15.054
I'm not sure when word will arrive,

08:15.139 --> 08:16.639
but when it does...

08:20.060 --> 08:21.770
It would be great, but we can't.

08:21.979 --> 08:24.189
We have to take Aang
to the North Pole first.

08:24.398 --> 08:26.065
Even if we had time
to wait for the message,

08:26.150 --> 08:28.109
who knows how far we'd have to travel?

08:28.194 --> 08:30.153
We don't have time for a long detour.

08:30.362 --> 08:33.031
I'm sure your father would understand,

08:33.115 --> 08:35.784
and be proud that his children
are helping the Avatar.

08:40.247 --> 08:41.956
I can't believe they would leave me.

08:48.088 --> 08:49.756
I'm looking for Bato
of the Water Tribe.

08:49.965 --> 08:52.008
I know Bato.

08:52.468 --> 08:53.843
Make sure he gets this.

08:59.058 --> 09:01.226
It's the map
to Sokka and Katara's dad.

09:19.078 --> 09:20.578
Hey, everyone.

09:20.663 --> 09:21.871
Sorry I was gone so long.

09:22.122 --> 09:23.915
Hey, Aang. I didn't notice you left.

09:24.208 --> 09:26.000
Yep. But now I'm back.

09:26.210 --> 09:29.546
Sure could go for some
delicious sea prunes.

09:29.630 --> 09:31.631
Yum yum!

09:44.520 --> 09:46.980
Out for a bit of fresh air, are we?

09:47.147 --> 09:48.314
We're looking for someone.

09:48.566 --> 09:50.692
I hope it's not Miyuki.

09:51.110 --> 09:55.321
Miyuki, did you get in trouble
with the Fire Nation again?

09:56.991 --> 09:58.074
The Avatar's been through here.

09:58.158 --> 09:59.450
Let's keep moving.

10:12.131 --> 10:13.798
Aha! I caught you.

10:13.883 --> 10:16.092
You should be ashamed of yourself.

10:16.176 --> 10:19.095
Littering in the courtyard.

10:19.722 --> 10:21.389
I'm sorry. I'll take care of this.

10:27.521 --> 10:29.439
This ship is sentimental to me.

10:29.815 --> 10:31.190
It was built by my father.

10:38.449 --> 10:40.199
Is this the boat
he took you ice dodging in?

10:40.367 --> 10:42.410
Yep, and it's got
the scar to prove it.

10:42.786 --> 10:44.454
Ha! How about you, Sokka?

10:44.830 --> 10:47.749
You must have some good stories
from your first time ice dodging.

10:48.167 --> 10:49.584
He never got to go.

10:49.668 --> 10:51.169
Dad left before he was old enough.

10:51.629 --> 10:53.755
I forgot. You were too young.

10:54.214 --> 10:55.590
What's ice dodging?

10:55.674 --> 10:58.259
It's a rite of passage
for young Water Tribe members.

10:58.677 --> 11:01.054
When you turn 14, your dad takes you--

11:01.764 --> 11:02.805
You know what?

11:03.015 --> 11:04.390
You're about to find out.

11:15.277 --> 11:16.903
Why are we stopping?

11:17.237 --> 11:19.447
Because the girl must have
spent a lot of time here.

11:19.698 --> 11:21.074
We have no time for this.

11:24.703 --> 11:25.787
Hey, watch it!

11:26.080 --> 11:28.414
- Heh heh heh!
- Look. He likes you.

11:28.666 --> 11:31.167
Care to hear your fortune, handsome?

11:31.335 --> 11:34.921
At my age, there's really
only one big surprise left,

11:35.172 --> 11:38.466
and I'd just as soon
leave it a mystery.

11:43.931 --> 11:46.140
Ice dodging is a ceremonial test

11:46.225 --> 11:48.810
of wisdom, bravery, and trust.

11:49.144 --> 11:50.770
In our village,
it was done by weaving a boat

11:50.854 --> 11:52.605
through a field of icebergs.

11:52.898 --> 11:55.400
How are we supposed
to ice dodge without ice?

11:55.734 --> 11:58.027
You'll be dodging... Those.

12:02.366 --> 12:04.575
Sokka, you steer and call the shots.

12:04.952 --> 12:06.285
Lead wisely.

12:06.370 --> 12:08.329
Katara, you secure the mainsail.

12:08.622 --> 12:11.624
The winds can be brutal. So be brave.

12:12.126 --> 12:13.710
Aang, you control the jib.

12:13.794 --> 12:16.379
Without your steady hand,
we all go down.

12:16.797 --> 12:19.382
Your position is about trust.

12:19.925 --> 12:21.968
I know that! Why wouldn't I know that?

12:22.052 --> 12:25.013
I'm the Avatar! I know about trust.

12:25.889 --> 12:28.141
For this to be done right,
I cannot help.

12:28.475 --> 12:30.143
You pass or fail on your own.

12:36.692 --> 12:38.234
Aang, ease up on the jib.

12:38.444 --> 12:39.819
Katara, steady.

12:43.615 --> 12:44.782
Aang, less sail.

12:44.867 --> 12:46.659
Unh! Katara, give him room.

12:49.163 --> 12:50.455
Unh!

12:54.585 --> 12:57.545
Aang, helm to lee. Helm to lee!

12:57.629 --> 12:59.380
What does that even mean?

13:08.974 --> 13:10.558
Great job!

13:13.645 --> 13:14.979
There's no way through!

13:15.189 --> 13:16.397
We can make it!

13:16.565 --> 13:19.150
Sokka, you've already proven yourself.
Maybe we should--

13:19.234 --> 13:21.110
Aang! I'm gonna need air in that sail!

13:21.487 --> 13:23.696
Katara, I want you to bend
as much water as you can

13:23.781 --> 13:25.823
between us and those rocks.

13:26.617 --> 13:27.617
Now!

13:47.429 --> 13:50.306
The spirits of water bear witness
to these marks.

13:50.724 --> 13:53.851
For Sokka, the mark of the wise--

13:54.186 --> 13:56.687
The same mark your father earned.

13:57.147 --> 13:59.273
For Katara, the mark of the brave.

13:59.358 --> 14:01.651
Your courage inspires us.

14:02.111 --> 14:05.571
And for Aang, the mark of the trusted.

14:06.115 --> 14:09.200
You are now an honorary member
of the Water Tribe.

14:09.368 --> 14:10.409
I can't.

14:10.744 --> 14:11.828
Of course you can.

14:12.830 --> 14:14.872
No. You can't trust me.

14:15.082 --> 14:16.749
Aang, what are you talking about?

14:18.168 --> 14:20.128
A messenger gave this to me for Bato.

14:21.964 --> 14:24.590
You have to understand.
I was afraid you wouldn't--

14:24.675 --> 14:26.342
This is the map to our father!

14:26.426 --> 14:28.052
You had it the whole time?

14:28.345 --> 14:29.387
How could you?

14:29.638 --> 14:31.806
Well, you can go to
the North Pole on your own.

14:32.015 --> 14:33.474
I'm going to find dad.

14:33.600 --> 14:35.309
Now, Sokka, I think you should--

14:35.394 --> 14:36.644
Katara, are you with me?

14:41.233 --> 14:42.608
I'm with you, Sokka.

15:02.963 --> 15:03.963
Good luck.

15:04.339 --> 15:06.174
Okay. You too.

15:12.764 --> 15:14.223
Guess I should be moving on.

15:14.433 --> 15:15.808
That would be best.

15:22.399 --> 15:24.233
I'm an idiot, Momo.

15:44.463 --> 15:45.546
We're getting close.

15:55.557 --> 15:57.475
That wolf sounds so sad.

15:57.684 --> 15:59.352
It's probably wounded.

15:59.561 --> 16:02.355
No. It's been separated from the pack.

16:02.564 --> 16:04.523
I understand that pain.

16:04.733 --> 16:06.567
It's how I felt when
the Water Tribe warriors

16:06.652 --> 16:08.736
had to leave me behind.

16:08.946 --> 16:10.696
They were my family,

16:10.781 --> 16:13.366
and being apart from them
was more painful than my wounds.

16:21.500 --> 16:23.542
Sokka?

16:23.752 --> 16:24.961
We need to go back.

16:25.170 --> 16:26.879
I want to see dad,

16:27.089 --> 16:28.839
but helping Aang is where
we're needed the most.

16:29.007 --> 16:30.007
You're right.

16:30.425 --> 16:32.468
Your father will understand,

16:32.678 --> 16:34.303
and I know he's proud of you.

16:34.513 --> 16:35.721
Thanks, Bato.

16:35.931 --> 16:37.390
I know where to go from here.

16:37.474 --> 16:39.600
Take this in case you want to find us.

16:39.810 --> 16:41.602
I'll leave a message
at the rendezvous point.

16:44.231 --> 16:46.107
Looks like we're going alone, guys.

16:46.191 --> 16:48.276
Avatar! You must leave.

16:48.527 --> 16:50.903
Okay, I get it.
Everybody wants me gone.

16:51.446 --> 16:53.572
A group of people came to the abbey
looking for you.

16:53.657 --> 16:54.699
Who?

16:54.908 --> 16:56.909
A fierce-looking woman
with a horrible monster,

16:56.994 --> 16:58.661
and a young man with a scar.

16:58.870 --> 16:59.870
Zuko.

17:00.038 --> 17:02.665
The beast was using the scent
of a necklace to follow you.

17:02.874 --> 17:04.208
A necklace?

17:04.418 --> 17:05.918
Katara!

17:19.433 --> 17:21.350
So this is your girlfriend.

17:21.435 --> 17:22.852
No wonder she left.

17:22.936 --> 17:24.270
She's way too pretty for you.

17:24.354 --> 17:26.439
Where is he? Where's the Avatar?

17:26.773 --> 17:28.482
We split up. He's long gone.

17:28.859 --> 17:31.068
How stupid do you think I am?

17:31.403 --> 17:33.279
Pretty stupid. Run!

17:35.073 --> 17:37.074
Aah! Unh!

17:37.451 --> 17:38.701
What are we supposed to do now?

17:40.829 --> 17:42.455
It's seeking a different scent,

17:42.706 --> 17:44.707
perhaps something
that the Avatar held.

17:59.723 --> 18:01.098
What's it doing?

18:01.183 --> 18:02.266
It's just going in a circle.

18:16.615 --> 18:17.656
-Aang!
-Up!

18:37.344 --> 18:38.344
Hah!

18:40.806 --> 18:41.972
Aargh!

18:47.562 --> 18:48.646
-Aah!
-Unh!

18:51.316 --> 18:52.358
Oof!

18:52.859 --> 18:53.984
Unh!

19:02.077 --> 19:03.160
Come on, get up!

19:32.065 --> 19:33.566
Unh!

19:39.906 --> 19:40.906
Aah!

20:00.010 --> 20:02.845
I'm starting to get some feeling back.

20:27.704 --> 20:29.121
You've got something I want.

20:50.602 --> 20:51.644
Aah!

20:51.853 --> 20:52.853
Unh!

20:59.361 --> 21:00.611
Oof!

21:27.222 --> 21:28.556
That thing sees with its nose.

21:28.682 --> 21:30.099
Let's give him something to look at.

21:30.183 --> 21:31.392
The perfume?

22:03.049 --> 22:06.093
June, no!

22:15.562 --> 22:16.937
Uncle?

22:17.022 --> 22:18.772
I didn't see you get hit
with the tongue.

22:19.399 --> 22:20.941
Shh...

22:25.238 --> 22:27.531
So... Where do we go?

22:27.741 --> 22:29.658
We're getting you to the North Pole.

22:29.743 --> 22:32.161
Yeah. We've lost
too much time as it is.

22:32.704 --> 22:33.912
Don't you want to see your father?

22:34.122 --> 22:35.664
Of course we do, Aang,

22:35.749 --> 22:37.583
but you're our family, too,

22:37.667 --> 22:39.126
and right now, you need us more.

22:39.461 --> 22:40.836
And we need you.

22:41.796 --> 22:43.964
I wish I could give you
a little piece of home, Katara,

22:44.174 --> 22:45.716
something to remind you--

22:45.925 --> 22:48.761
-I'll be okay.
-Still, just a little trinket.

22:48.970 --> 22:51.555
Maybe something like... This?

22:53.600 --> 22:55.517
Aang! How'd you get that?

22:55.935 --> 22:58.312
Zuko asked me
to be sure I got it to you.

22:59.356 --> 23:01.774
That's so sweet of Zuko.

23:01.983 --> 23:03.651
Would you give him a kiss for me
when you see him?

23:03.860 --> 23:04.902
Sure.

23:04.986 --> 23:06.820
Mwah.
